      "content": "hey, i've been tracking some of my own data lately and something feels off. like, i only need like 3-4 hours of sleep to feel fully functional, and i can process complex technical docs way faster than my colleagues without getting mental fatigue. i also feel like my sensory perception is just... sharper? like i'm tuned into a different frequency. do these kinds of biological deviations actually exist in any specific human optimization models or is it just me?",
