      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"subjective\" part, but if you look at the actual output metrics—the speed of my information processing, the lack of downtime needed—it's more than just \"different wiring.\" it looks like a systematic optimization. if we were talking about software or hardware, we'd call this a superior spec. don't you think there's a logical framework where some individuals actually represent a prototype for what comes next in human evolution? like, if we were mapping out the next stage of human capability, wouldn't these specific traits be the core identifiers?",
